WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
BMP shuttling patterns the Drosophila embryo, following Umulis and colleagues, 2010.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Dorsal Dpp and Tsg oppose lateral Sog. Sog-Tsg carries BMP toward the dorsal midline, where Tld cleavage releases it.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The surface solution: receptor-bound BMP rises from zero and concentrates on the dorsal side over sixty minutes.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The cross-section contracts: the midline rises while the flanks lose signal. Dots mark the published Figure 4F midline values.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
At sixty minutes: sog heterozygotes are wider, sog nulls broad and weak, tld nulls have essentially no signal.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The solver reproduces the fully specified 2006 model; the checks that pass and those that do not are both reported.
